The Snake game, terminal renderer, replay tools and cycle-safety mechanism
originate there. K3 changes include a Laya SDK backend, fixed SpaceMIT ONNX
FP16 offload, optional auxiliary estimates, startup/threads tuning, local
compatibility adaptation, packaging and installation verification.

The upstream project includes software derived from Laya:
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
Copyright Convai Innovations and Laya contributors, Apache-2.0.
Upstream source revision cited by laya-mlx:
6a5819129eb220570792e417e49723d697efd76f.
The token sequence construction, question rendering, confidence calculation,
presets, email utilities and language router are adapted from Laya.
The upstream neural network is reimplemented using Apple's MLX, following
Laya's DecisionModel and ModernBERT in Hugging Face Transformers. This K3
distribution does not run that Apple MLX backend; it calls the Laya SDK or
the separately downloaded community ONNX model.

Model weights are NOT distributed in this repository or application package.
The download manifest links to Convai Innovations and mizchi on Hugging Face.

Binary releases bundle unmodified Python wheels listed in
requirements-runtime.txt. Their license notices are retained in each wheel.
The tokenizers 0.22.2 riscv64 wheel was built locally from the upstream
release without source modifications; its Apache-2.0 license is also supplied
in docs/licenses/tokenizers-LICENSE. See docs/THIRD_PARTY.md.
